mothershipOS: the virtio keyboard also declares KEY_WAKEUP. Its key bitmap had KEY_POWER but not KEY_WAKEUP, so the
guest's input core dropped every KEY_WAKEUP the host sent: mship-inputd's wake when it lends the display, and the
touchscreen's wake gesture (double tap while the panel is off). KEY_WAKEUP wakes the guest without toggling its
screen (KEY_POWER would put an awake guest to sleep).

diff --git a/devices/src/virtio/input/defaults.rs b/devices/src/virtio/input/defaults.rs
index 23014baa0..eb9e9529d 100644
--- a/devices/src/virtio/input/defaults.rs
+++ b/devices/src/virtio/input/defaults.rs
@@ -444,6 +444,9 @@ fn default_keyboard_events() -> BTreeMap<u16, virtio_input_bitmap> {
             KEY_MENU,
             KEY_PRINT,
             KEY_POWER,
+            // mothershipOS: wakes the guest without toggling its screen (a touchscreen wake gesture, the host
+            // lending the display); KEY_POWER would put an awake guest to sleep
+            KEY_WAKEUP,
             KEY_HOMEPAGE,
             KEY_MUTE,
             KEY_VOLUMEDOWN,
